# a ± b of numbers is an interval, worst-case bounds (notes/plus_minus.md P217), printed to 2 significant digits of its ± part (P219)
'use uncertain; str(6.0 ± 0.3)'	'6.00 ± 0.30'
'use uncertain; str((5 ± 1) + (2 ± 1))'	'7.0 ± 2.0'
'use uncertain; x = 5 ± 1; str(x - x)'	'0.0 ± 2.0'
'use uncertain; str((6.0 ± 0.3) * 2)'	'12.00 ± 0.60'
'use uncertain; (3 ± 0.5).high'	3.5
'use uncertain; (3 ± 0.5).low'	2.5
